  "body": "Setup sheet tool list now prints a tool's stated part number, vendor, coating and helix angle.\n\n**Stacked on #1070 (#898)**, which adds the fields; its commits show in this diff until it merges. Retarget/merge main after #1070 lands. Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\nWhat changed: `crates/app/src/setup_sheet/tools.rs` adds one line under each tool's geometry line, e.g. `PART XY-1234  VENDOR Acme Tooling  HELIX 35.000 deg`. Fixed order part, vendor, coating, helix; unstated facts omitted whole (no \"None\", no empty labels); a tool stating none gets no line. Notes are not printed. The setup sheet module writes plain text only, so there is no HTML/PDF path to change. Display only: no posted G-code change. Decision: `docs/decisions/1063-sheet-tool-catalog-fields.md`.\n\nPinned by: `setup_sheet::tool_list_prints_stated_catalog_facts_and_omits_unstated` (one tool stating part/vendor/helix with coating unstated, one tool stating nothing). No existing sheet output changes: no other tool states facts, and no golden holds a sheet with them.\n\nTested: `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test setup_sheet` (8 passed); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. Not exercised: the other suites that render sheets (setup_align, setup_wcs, etc.; unaffected since their tools state no facts), the ui crate.\n\nChangelog: Setup sheet tool list prints part number, vendor, coating and helix when stated (#1063)\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1063\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
